22:19.195 --> 22:28.839
[SPEAKER_01]: everybody should have a flight log. But I have a kiting log also. Every single kiting session that I do, I log which wing I used, where was it, how

22:28.859 --> 22:37.683
[SPEAKER_01]: many hours did I ground handle. And I maintain my ground handling log even now. And I finished that first year and I went back to Mitch and said,

22:37.723 --> 22:44.366
[SPEAKER_01]: hey, Mitch, you'll be disappointed because I couldn't do the 52 hours. I got to 39 hours. And he's like, hey, I was just giving you a bluff because

22:44.546 --> 22:55.254
[SPEAKER_01]: 39 is great. It's awesome. And I was like, okay, cool. But there is a sense of, I think, discipline that is helpful in a lot of aspects of prior

22:55.274 --> 23:02.837
[SPEAKER_01]: learning. As long as you have the motivation, it's just working out. You might envision a great body. But if you don't work out, you won't have it.

23:03.057 --> 23:12.685
[SPEAKER_01]: And likewise, in paragliding, you aspire to be a good pilot, but it just takes a lot of work and dedication. It's like going to the gym so you can

